      "name": "YT: RETRIEVE COMMENTS",
      "credentials": {
        "youTubeOAuth2Api": {
          "id": "L3nuPjdrJiQamOpM",
          "name": "n8n-justin-youtube-account"
        }
      },
      "notes": "GET https://www.googleapis.com/youtube/v3/commentThreads\n\n- Give me the comments/comment threads that match my request.\n\nWhat does part=snippet mean? \n\n- For commentThreads, the available parts include: id, snippet, replies (but we don't retrieve the replies in this case)\n\n- you're asking YouTube to return the basic information about each comment thread.\n\nWhat does maxResults=100 mean?\n\n- Give me a maximum of 100 comment threads in this API response.\n- For example, if the video has 2,500 comments and you use maxResults=100 You don't get all 2,500 comments.\n- Then YouTube gives you a \"nextPageToken\": \"...\" You use that token to get the next 100.\n\n--\n\nVIDEO ID:\n- can handle https://youtu.be/fWssgnf6fOY?si=KAXDuFmg96bPuFZi OR https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4Bb20KFo89A auto splice to get the id from URL\n\n--\n\nMAX PAGE IS 50 MEANING WE ONLY RETRIEVE 5,000 COMMENTS (50X100) \n\nENABLE PAGINATION OPTION TO RETRIEVE ALL COMMENTS\n\n- keep paginating as long as nextPageToken exists in the response; stop once it's missing\n"
    }
